window.MM_SEARCH=[{"p":"changelog.html","t":"Changelog","s":[{"id":"h.2ac3c30c11598da_48","h":"The changelog here will no longer be updated. Please join the Discord to view the changelogs.","x":"The changelog here will no longer be updated. Please join the Discord to view the changelogs."},{"id":"h.2ac3c30c11598da_58","h":"","x":"Join the Discord!"},{"id":"h.2ac3c30c11598da_62","h":"Old versions of the Megathread","x":"Old versions of the Megathread"},{"id":"h.2ac3c30c11598da_66","h":"Notionthread (v3)","x":"Notionthread (v3)"},{"id":"h.2ac3c30c11598da_74","h":"","x":"Notionthread download Mirrors: Mirror #1, Mirror #2"},{"id":"h.67961db8c638d02e_0","h":"Google Docs Megathread (v2)","x":"Google Docs Megathread (v2) Download Mirrors: Mirror #1, Mirror #2"},{"id":"h.4f20cf7472b93348_7","h":"","x":"MCSM Megathread"},{"id":"h.804d0d2aa297c74_4","h":"Original Reddit Megathread (v1)","x":"Original Reddit Megathread (v1)"},{"id":"h.670de979332aef5a_9","h":"Original Reddit Megathread (WARNING: REALLY BAD) Click to expand","x":"Original Reddit Megathread (WARNING: REALLY BAD) Click to expand Hello everyone, Unfortunately nothing built can last forever. So eventually Minecraft Story Mode got shut down. I recently saw a post talking about how annoying the posts are asking how to get the game in 2023. So I’ve decided to make a megathread. Yes, this guide will involve sailing the seven seas but I’ll provide alternatives if you don’t want to p!rate (not recommended, it costs an arm and a leg, you aren’t supporting the devs and you’re risking getting scammed). Mods, plz don’t ban me, it’s impossible to get the game properly right now, even if you don’t p!rate the game, you’re just helping greedy scalpers, Telltale and Mojang will not profit. This post will reduce the stream of “guys hoe i get in android phone” and prevent misinformation. Let’s get started. About each version of the game Normal disc that just says “Minecraft Story Mode” contains the first 5 episodes of season 1. These episodes are not on the disc (apart from Episode 1) so if you’re purchasing for a console with a shut down store (currently only Xbox 360, though PS3 could be soon) you won’t be able to play the other episodes. “Complete Adventure” disc/cartridge contains all the episodes for Season 1. (Only version available of Season 1 for Wii U and Switch) this version contains all of the Episodes on disc, so buying for Xbox 360 is ok. “Minecraft Story Mode Season Two” disc/cartridge is the second season of the game. The episodes need to be downloaded so again, if you’re on a console with a discontinued store (Xbox 360) you can only play episode one. This is not available for PS3. Sites Referenced Myrient = https://myrient.erista.me Mariocube = https://mariocube.com Steamunlocked = SIKE! Do not use this site Amazon = https://Amazon.com EBay = https://eBay.com Mercari = SIKE! This site is crawling with scammers. Do not use this site. rpgonly = https://rpgonly.com nxbrew = https://nxbrew.com Adblockers Ublock Origin is a free adblocker, trusted by google and has over 10 million users. https://ublock.org VPNs Proton VPN is by far the best VPN. All free VPNs share your data in some way so use at your own risk. https://protonvpn.com Surfshark is a great paid VPN that is still cheap. https://surfshark.com/ Nord VPN is a luxury. It’s expensive but it’s by far the best. https://nordvpn.com HOW TO GET MCSM CURRENTLY Xbox 360 Physical Discs Currently, the Complete Adventure is the only disc that will work physically. Homebrew Using a game rom taken from a site (Myrient is the one I recommend and use) you can run the game via JTAG off a usb. You can also run a patch for Season 2 to get all of the episodes. PS3 Physical Discs Complete Adventure Disc is the only version to get unless you’re collecting, or can’t spare an extra ten bucks or so. Buy it off ebay or another trusted site of your choice. Avoid mercari because it’s notorious for scams. Homebrew Download the Complete Adventure .iso off of Myrient. You’ll need to decrypt the iso by mounting it with an iso mounting software, use PS3 ISO Dumper to dump the game files and use PS3 ISO Tools to compile it back to iso. Use FTP transferring to your PS3 and boot it via MultiMAN or play it on a USB/External Hard Drive via WebMAN. Xbox One Physical Discs Any disc will work, no problems here. Homebrew Nothing is possible here PS4 Physical Discs Again, all discs work Homebrew You’d need a jailbreakable PS4. Here is a good guide to hack a PS4 https://wololo.net/ps4-jailbreak-ps4-cfw4dummies/ Get a rom here https://gamesmega.net/ or t0rrent here https://www.gamestorrents.nu/ Wii U Physical Discs Complete Adventure works fine. It’s the only release for the system so really not much to say here. Homebrew Wii U USB Helper will work for the Complete Adventure. You can alternatively download the rom from Mariocube or Myrient Nintendo Switch Cartridges All cartridges work but they’re extremely expensive. Buy them off of Amazon or another trusted site. Homebrew Use a hacked/modchipped Switch to run tinfoil and boot the .xci file. You could try downloading the S2 episodes via a burner account but it will likely get banned. I’d recommend getting the games from nxbrew.com or nsw2u.xyz , make sure you use an adblocker! iOS Use Cydia Impactor on a jailbroken device to run the .ipa with the episodes patch. Ipa sites are constantly going down so you’ll need your own research here. You also need the latest version because most of the older versions are 32-bit. Android Download a .xapk and download an xapk installer from the Play Store. You can find an apk search engine in r/FREEMEDIAHECKYEAH no need to download the episodes, both seasons should have them there. Mac You need to get a cracked version. You can find it from https://rentry.org/pgames Windows Legally You can buy a rom disc off of Amazon, EBay or another trusted site. No, Steam keys are not legit. You may get your account suspended, the game taken and you also can easily get scammed. Yarr! Download off of Steamrip.com Alternatively you can t0rrent off of fitgirl-repacks. Use an adblocker and if you’re torrenting - a VPN (virtual private network) DO NOT USE STEAMUNLOCKED The site used to be semi-alright but they’ve implemented adware hijackers into their site, malicious redirects, broken Repacks, stolen Repacks and they usually steal from IGG Games which: Put DRM in their games which prevents the files being copied Put ads in their games Hide cryptominers in their games And make malware activate at startup While the MCSM repack has been deemed safe, you can still get the adware hijackers and of course the malicious redirects not to mention the terrible download speed. Netflix Version The MCSM Netflix Archive has you covered. Two out of five episodes are done as of right now. You can view their content here https://m.youtube.com/@minecraftstorymodenetflix/videos Phew! That was a lot, I hope this helps you on your journey, adventurers! Changelog 3/8/23 Corrected Wii U section to remove Season 2 Added Adblocker/VPN section Added site index 4/8/23 Added the PS4 Homebrew Section 21/8/23 Added Netflix Section Tweaked PS3 section 30/8/23 Fixed minor mistake in the “About each version of the game” section 15/9/23 Grammar fixes"},{"id":"h.704885ebc648004b_3","h":"","x":"The Minecraft: Story Mode Megathread, by the Megathread Team. This is a fanmade project, not affiliated with Mojang or Telltale Games in any way.If info from this site is used, please give credit. Note that anything on the site is subject to change, be safe on the internet! Megathread v4.1 | Made in Google Sites, domain hosted by GoDaddy"}]},{"p":"index.html","t":"Start","s":[{"id":"h.49d7045630b4eb6_13","h":"Welcome to the FEAR's Megathread!","x":"Welcome to the FEAR's Megathread! Welcome! This is a giant guide that will teach you all about how to get games that were removed from storefronts. I often see people getting tricked by misinformation or clicking random links in hopes that they can play the game again, so that's why this website exists, to help stop misinformation and for you to learn how to obtain the game free and safely. While your here consider joining the discord!"},{"id":"h.2ee3d3d9ca8851da_30","h":"IMPORTANT!","x":"IMPORTANT! Read below if nothing else. These things are very important for the rest of the guide."},{"id":"h.2ee3d3d9ca8851da_31","h":"Ad-blocker(s)","x":"Ad-blocker(s)"},{"id":"h.2ee3d3d9ca8851da_68","h":"","x":"uBlock Origin is a free, open-source, up-to-date ad-blocker with over 10 million users. This is by far the best and only ad-blocker we'd recommend. An ad-blocker is a good thing to have when going on certain sites. Ads are how websites make their money, and people are often blinded by money. Most sites nowadays bombard the user with ads to the point that the main content is overshadowed. They'll often appear as fake download buttons, please either use an ad-blocker or your brain to avoid clicking these."},{"id":"h.2ee3d3d9ca8851da_69","h":"VPN's (Virtual Private Network)","x":"VPN's (Virtual Private Network)"},{"id":"h.2ee3d3d9ca8851da_76","h":"","x":"Surfshark is a great paid VPN that is still cheap. Nord VPN is a luxury. It’s expensive but it’s by far the best. Mullvad VPN is a great and simple, very privacy focused VPN. Prices range from cheap to fair, and they all give you the same features, just for a differing amount of time. Torrenting is a decentralized way to download files. Instead of downloading a file directly from a server, it's downloaded from other's computers with the same files. A common misconception is that torrenting itself is illegal, which it's not. It's just another way of downloading things and is usually faster when dealing with large files. Although, what most people use it for is piracy, which is where it gets it's reputation. A VPN is necessary because, in the case of our abandonware, you are technically committing piracy, and while torrenting, your ISP (Internet Service Provider) can see everything. While our beliefs of these games being abandonware (not able to purchase realistically anymore) make this more or less justified, your ISP only sees what you're doing at face value. Better to be safe than sorry. If this sounds kind of scary, if you choose to direct-download (download through your browser, not through a torrent client), you don't have to worry about this. DO NOT use free VPN's when torrenting, they all sell your data in some way, so use at your own risk. Most don't usually support peer-to-peer connections anyway."},{"id":"h.251d374b79b45c7b_0","h":"Please note that YOU and ONLY YOU are responsible for any complaints you get from your ISP for torrenting or otherwise.","x":"Please note that YOU and ONLY YOU are responsible for any complaints you get from your ISP for torrenting or otherwise."},{"id":"h.new_sj4829ob4cfq","h":"","x":"First item Second item Third item Fourth item Fifth item Sixth item Seventh item Eighth item Ninth item Tenth item"}]},{"p":"others-pc-games.html","t":"Games","s":[{"id":"h.new_mjgiurxp0gek","h":"Abandon-ware Games","x":"Abandon-ware Games Steven universe: Attack the light + Steven universe: Save the light + Steven universe: Unleash the light can be found in Google Drive (only Save the light was virus checked by hand) Provided by @TheRedJinty & @the_bitrex on twitter"},{"id":"h.new_9aiuj6j1aizv","h":"","x":"Adventure Time: Explore the Dungeon Because I Don't Know! Can be found in Internet Archive (all files were checked by hand. deemed safe with multi-able false positives) Provided by Gintoku on Internet Archive"}]}];
